 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "00436068",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Tau-5* SEC-SAXS: clean-window selection, standard plots and EFA\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook accompanies the files in `poster_results/`. It uses the requested WT_092025 and AA_052026 HDF5 series. The original source notebooks remain unchanged. The selected windows are **WT 159–175** and **AA 169–188**, inclusive and zero indexed. See `EFA_report.md` for biological interpretation and `EFA_equations.md` for the full equation walkthrough.\n",
    "\n",
    "No oligomeric identity is assigned from Rg alone. Window scores are a presentation-quality criterion conditional on the supplied errors and chosen residual-background correction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "666b54c5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:17:29.718276Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:17:29.718106Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.222162Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.221711Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import sys, json, numpy as np\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'analysis'))\n",
    "from run_efa import analyze, guinier\n",
    "from select_windows import average, candidates\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Image, Markdown\n",
    "assert (ROOT / 'BNL_SAXS/data/WT_092025.hdf5').exists()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "01bf9483",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Verify the WT construct\n",
    "\n",
    "Your exact supplied sequence is the experimental reference. It has 120 residues, including the N-terminal GP; the segment after GP has 118. BMRB53105 is a 119-residue Tau-5* construct. The user sequence adds GP and removes its terminal C. User W70/W106 correspond to AR W397/W433. Expected WT monomer mass is the user-supplied 12.1 kDa."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "b837f407",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.223446Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.223355Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.228747Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.228376Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "{'user_length': 120,\n",
       " 'bmrb_length': 119,\n",
       " 'relationship': 'user = GP + BMRB53105 sequence without terminal C',\n",
       " 'expected_monomer_mass_kDa': 12.1,\n",
       " 'sequence_1_based_W_positions': [70, 106],\n",
       " 'AR_W_positions': [397, 433],\n",
       " 'mapping': 'User positions 3–120 match BMRB positions 1–118 and author AR positions 330–447 of BMRB51479.',\n",
       " 'source': 'https://bmrb.io/ftp/pub/bmrb/entry_directories/bmr53105/bmr53105_3.str'}"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 2,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "sequence_info = json.loads((ROOT/'background/sequence_comparison.json').read_text())\n",
    "sequence_info\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f0953d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Recompute the selected averaging windows\n",
    "\n",
    "Candidates contain the local SEC maximum, have at least seven frames, and lie inside WT 150–195 or AA 155–215. Passing criteria: ≤5% Rg span over four low-q cutoffs, Guinier reduced weighted residual ≤1.5, and amplitude-scaled first/second-half profile residual mean square ≤1.5. Among passing candidates we maximize the mean-profile signal/error norm. Shared residual-background uncertainty is retained when averaging.\n",
    "\n",
    "The optimization does not use a target Rg. Neighboring windows are nearly tied."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "738b48ce",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.229632Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.229584Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.907851Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.907583Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "WT_092025 evaluated: 475 selected: 159 175 Rg: 25.791 A qmin span: 1.43 %\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "AA_052026 evaluated: 876 selected: 169 188 Rg: 32.346 A qmin span: 2.68 %\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "selection = []\n",
    "for name, lo, hi in [('WT_092025',150,195), ('AA_052026',155,215)]:\n",
    "    rows, best = candidates(name, lo, hi)\n",
    "    selection.append(best)\n",
    "    print(name, 'evaluated:',len(rows), 'selected:',best['start'],best['end'],\n",
    "          'Rg:',round(best['Rg'],3), 'A', 'qmin span:',round(100*best['qmin_Rg_relative_span'],2),'%')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "3b1ee6e5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
