   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe572d64",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Arithmetic mean profiles and Guinier fits\n",
    "\n",
    "The Guinier relation is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\ln I(q)=\\ln I(0)-\\frac{R_g^2}{3}q^2,$$\n",
    "\n",
    "so a fitted slope m gives $R_g=\\sqrt{-3m}$. The primary fit starts at q=0.012 Å⁻¹ and enforces qmax Rg≤1. Points excluded from the fitted range are gray in the plots. Fit errors are conditional and exclude background-choice systematics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "4f35b0ee",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.913463Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.913400Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.942283Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:17:30.942022Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "WT_092025 {'Rg': 25.79130298737548, 'fit_se': 0.5843627653960966, 'I0': 1.6670910507471233, 'qmin': 0.012, 'qmax': 0.038, 'qRgmax': 0.9800695135202683, 'n': 27, 'chi2': 0.4983256226424583}\n",
      "AA_052026 {'Rg': 32.346301385479485, 'fit_se': 0.5086195640714725, 'I0': 4.749794588648265, 'qmin': 0.012, 'qmax': 0.030000000000000002, 'qRgmax': 0.9703890415643847, 'n': 19, 'chi2': 0.4816581181110445}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "guinier_results = {}\n",
    "for s in selection:\n",
    "    q, intensity, error = average(s['sample'],s['start'],s['end'])\n",
    "    fit = guinier(q,intensity,error)\n",
    "    guinier_results[s['sample']] = fit\n",
    "    print(s['sample'], fit)\n"
   ]
  },
